const support=(route,title,content)=>layout({route,title:title==='About PrintCost Studio'?title:title+' | PrintCost Studio',description:supportDescriptions[route],active:'',article:true,main:`<div class="container"><article class="editorial"><h1>${escape(title)}</h1>${content}</article></div>`});
const privacy=()=>support('/privacy/','Privacy Policy',`<p>PrintCost Studio is designed so that entered calculation values are processed in your browser. The current site does not transmit your print parameters to an application server, does not require user accounts and does not use paid APIs.</p><h2>Local storage</h2><p>By default, the calculator saves your latest input values in browser <code>localStorage</code> under <code>printcost.studio.settings.v1</code>. Uncheck <strong>Remember my inputs on this device</strong> under the calculator to delete saved inputs immediately and stop saving new values. The separate preference <code>printcost.studio.remember.v1</code> records your decision to leave saving disabled, but contains no print settings or prices. Reset deletes saved inputs and restores example values without changing your saving preference. You can also clear all data through your browser's site-data controls. Saved values do not sync across devices.</p><h2>Hosting and network traffic</h2><p>Opening the website still sends ordinary HTTP requests to the site's hosting provider, which may process IP addresses and standard request metadata. The calculator itself has no advertising trackers, third-party fonts, cookies set by our application or uploaded print-file processing. Cloudflare Web Analytics is currently enabled by the hosting configuration and may automatically inject a performance beacon loaded from <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js</code>. According to <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/data-origin-and-collection/">Cloudflare Web Analytics documentation</a>, this beacon measures page-view and performance timing data; it is separate from the calculator logic and does not require us to send your entered print settings to an application server. Cloudflare controls and processes the resulting analytics data. The site operator can disable the beacon in Cloudflare Web Analytics settings. Any future advertising or analytics changes will require a new privacy review.</p><h2>Estimates</h2><p>Your input values stay in your browser; downloaded CSV files and printouts are saved using your device. Calculation results are estimates, not verified purchase prices or financial advice.</p><p>Privacy notice last reviewed: November 3, 2026. For privacy inquiries or corrections, email <a href="mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}">${CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You may also report non-sensitive bugs through the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/3D-Printing/issues/new">public GitHub issue tracker</a>; do not include confidential orders or personal details in public issues.</p>`);
const about=()=>support('/about/','About PrintCost Studio',`<p>PrintCost Studio is an independent cost and pricing calculator for people running FDM desktop 3D printers. Its purpose is to make the arithmetic transparent: filament, electricity, useful-life machine allocation, active labor, failure losses and order fees.</p><h2>What the calculator does</h2><p>Users provide their own printer and material assumptions; the tool computes estimates locally. It does not claim to measure a printer's actual energy usage, know a marketplace's current charges or replace a professional business quotation.</p><h2>What this project does not claim</h2><p>The site does not claim official affiliation with Prusa, PrintPal, Creality, Bambu Lab or other 3D printing companies. Examples are illustrative. No user counts, qualifications, testimonials or earnings are represented as verified facts.</p><h2>Who publishes these methods?</h2><p><strong>PrintCost Studio</strong> is this independent website’s publishing brand. It does not claim registered corporate status, engineering certifications, a manufacturer partnership or third-party laboratory testing. Our examples are first-party calculations that can be reproduced using the disclosed inputs.</p><h2>Public implementation</h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/3D-Printing">public GitHub project repository</a> contains the site source and issue history. This is first-party implementation evidence, not an independent certification.</p><h2>Methods</h2><p>Calculation formulas and a fully worked example are published on the <a href="/calculation-methodology/">calculation methodology page</a>. Material, power, printer life and fee assumptions can be edited before exporting a quote. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> to understand local storage. For direct support, email <a href="mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}">${CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>`);
const terms=()=>support('/terms/','Terms of Use',`<p><strong>PrintCost Studio provides free FDM printing cost and selling-price estimates from your inputs.</strong> This is a planning aid, not a verified quote, invoice, tax calculation or professional assessment.</p><h2>Using the calculators</h2><p>Review the actual material, time, power, labor, failure, shipping and fee assumptions before you use an estimate commercially. No signup, subscription or payment is required for the current tools.</p><h2>What the estimates include</h2><p>Our <a href="/calculation-methodology/">methodology</a> describes the mathematical assumptions, with reproducible examples. Actual print failures, material waste, maintenance and third-party fees may differ. Taxes and costs you have not entered are not automatically included.</p><h2>Availability and data</h2><p>There is no promise of uninterrupted access or suitability for a specific production operation. Calculations run locally in your browser; see <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for stored settings and hosting information.</p><h2>Corrections and support</h2><p>For a reproducible error, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or the public <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/3D-Printing/issues/new">GitHub tracker</a>. Avoid publishing confidential order data. Terms last reviewed November 3, 2026.</p>`);
const contact=()=>support('/contact/','Contact & Support',`<p>For private inquiries or calculator support, email <a href="mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}">${CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. This is our designated contact address. Email delivery depends on the domain's mail-provider DNS and mailbox setup; do not include passwords or confidential customer files.</p><p>For calculator issues, describe the input values, expected result and browser version so the computation can be reproduced. If you prefer a public bug report, <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/3D-Printing/issues/new">open an issue on GitHub</a> (a GitHub account may be required); you may also review <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/3D-Printing/issues">existing public issues</a>.</p><p>GitHub Issues are public. Never share private customer details or confidential orders in an issue. Review <a href="/calculation-methodology/">the calculation methods</a> for assumptions and formulas.</p>`);
